{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, thanks. I’ve been having this pain in my upper belly, mostly on the right side and near my stomach. It’s worse the last two days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Is it different from your usual G-tube pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, this feels deeper, more like a burning in my upper belly. It reminds me of when I had that ulcer before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned you ran out of oxycodone—have you taken anything for the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just Tylenol, but it didn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll get you something for pain. You’re still on your tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, at 40 cc/hour. No vomiting or diarrhea. But I think the feed is leaking around the tube a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check the site. Any fever, chills, or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or breathing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re going to keep you on bowel rest for now, give you IV fluids, and start a medication called pantoprazole to reduce stomach acid. We also ordered an ultrasound of your gallbladder and liver to rule out other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve had that ultrasound before—last time it was fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we just got the results. No gallstones or gallbladder inflammation. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing the pain then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history, we think it might be a recurrence of your marginal ulcer—the kind that can happen after gastric bypass. That’s why we’re using the acid blocker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. That makes sense. I’ve been stressed lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2173-11-15 19:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stress can play a role. We’ll also check your labs to make sure there’s no infection or other issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night show your white blood cell count was a bit high yesterday evening but came down. Liver and pancreas enzymes are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a sign of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The rise could be from inflammation or stress on the body. But no fever, and your other markers look good. We don’t think it’s an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my lactate was high—what does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was mildly elevated, which can happen with pain or dehydration. It’s improving, so we’re not concerned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Can I start drinking water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start you on small sips. And we’re adding a medication called sucralfate—it coats the ulcer and helps it heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that the same as before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2173-11-16 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s often used for ulcers like yours. We’ll keep the IV pantoprazole for now and transition to oral meds soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2173-11-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2173-11-16 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I haven’t needed any strong pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2173-11-16 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll restart your tube feeds at 50 cc/hour and keep you on water by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2173-11-16 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my G-tube—I’m supposed to get it replaced soon, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2173-11-16 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your surgeon has scheduled the revision. We’re making sure the ulcer is under control first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2173-11-16 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been anxious about it. I feel like it’s taking forever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2173-11-16 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We want to do it safely, especially with the ulcer. But you’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we’re discharging you today. Your pain has improved, and you’re tolerating feeds and water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds will I be on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue lansoprazole twice daily, sucralfate four times a day, and oxycodone liquid for breakthrough pain. Also, keep taking your fluoxetine, rifaximin, and other home meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, NutriHep at 50 cc/hour. Monitor the G-tube site for redness, swelling, or increased pain. Call your surgeon if you notice anything unusual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if the pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the oxycodone as needed. But if it’s not helping, or if you have fever, vomiting, or severe bloating, go to the ER or call your surgeon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I’ll keep avoiding NSAIDs, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. No NSAIDs, alcohol, or smoking. They can worsen ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in follow-up, and your G-tube surgery is coming up soon. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2173-11-17 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Dr. Lee."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2173-11-15 18:49:00",
    "admission_end": "2173-11-17 13:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for acute abdominal pain in the epigastric and right upper quadrant, distinct from her chronic G-tube site pain and suggestive of a recurrent marginal ulcer. She had run out of oxycodone and found minimal relief with acetaminophen. An ultrasound ruled out cholecystitis, and labs showed transient leukocytosis and elevated lactate, both resolving without signs of infection. She was managed with bowel rest, IV fluids, IV pantoprazole, and later sucralfate, with significant improvement in pain. She resumed tube feeds and oral intake, remained stable, and was discharged home with a plan to continue acid suppression and sucralfate, along with scheduled G-tube revision surgery. Discharge instructions emphasized medication adherence, avoidance of NSAIDs, and monitoring for warning symptoms.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Bariatric surgery status"
    ]
  }
}
